---
import BlogLayout from '../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro';
import CopyButton from '../../components/CopyButton.astro';
import { authoredBlogMetadata, formatBlogDate } from '../../data/blogPresentation';
import { createBreadcrumbSchema, productFacts } from '../../data/productFacts';

const title = 'Stop Paranoid Debugging: 1-Second Cloud State Resets';
const description = 'Stop wasting hours debugging phantom errors from dirty staging data. Reset local GCP state and restore deterministic YAML fixtures in under a second.';
const pageUrl = new URL('blog/one-second-cloud-state-resets/', productFacts.siteUrl).toString();
const metadata = authoredBlogMetadata['one-second-cloud-state-resets'];
const contents = [
  { id: 'problem', label: 'The hidden cost of dirty test state' },
  { id: 'solution', label: 'Deterministic baselines with seed.yaml' },
  { id: 'reset-routes', label: 'Reset and reseed in under a second' },
  { id: 'try-it', label: 'Test a fast reset cycle' },
  { id: 'checklist', label: 'Keep fixture resets honest' },
];
const seedYaml = `services:
  gcs:
    buckets:
      - name: exports-baseline
        objects:
          - key: fixtures/sample.csv
            content: "id,status\\n1,active\\n"
  pubsub:
    topics:
      - name: orders-topic
        subscriptions:
          - name: orders-sub`;
const resetCmd = `# Load your baseline fixtures
curl -fsS -X POST http://localhost:5380/seed \\
  -H 'Content-Type: application/yaml' \\
  --data-binary @seed.yaml

# Later: clear project state and restore the most recent seed (~380 ms)
curl -fsS -X POST 'http://localhost:5380/reset?project=local-gcp-project' \\
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\
  -d '{"restore_seed":true}'`;
const structuredData = [
  createBreadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', url: productFacts.siteUrl },
    { name: 'Blog', url: new URL('blog/', productFacts.siteUrl).toString() },
    { name: title, url: pageUrl },
  ]),
];
---

<BlogLayout {title} {description} {structuredData} {contents} article={{ publishedAt: metadata.publishedAt, headline: title }}>
  <Fragment slot="hero">
    <article class="site-section site-section--hero">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <nav class="mb-5 text-sm text-[var(--text-2)]" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/blog/">Blog</a></nav>
        <span class="site-eyebrow">Developer Productivity</span>
        <h1 class="mt-5">{title}</h1>
        <p class="blog-meta"><span>Published <time datetime={metadata.publishedAt}>{formatBlogDate(metadata.publishedAt)}</time></span><span>{metadata.minutes} min read</span><span>{metadata.topic}</span></p>
        <p class="blog-deck">Half of integration debugging goes to figuring out whether your code broke or yesterday’s leftover rows corrupted the environment. Snap back to a clean fixture baseline in ~380 ms.</p>
        <div class="blog-actions">
          <a class="site-button site-button--primary" href="/docs/seed-data/">Seed data reference</a>
          <a href="/docs/">Quick start</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </Fragment>

  <section class="site-section">
    <div class="container container--narrow space-y-10">
      <section>
        <h2 id="problem">The hidden cost of dirty test state</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">“Did my refactor fail, or did an earlier test leave a duplicate primary key in Spanner and an unacknowledged message in Pub/Sub?” That uncertainty triggers slow manual cleanup scripts, ad-hoc bucket deletes, and paranoid re-runs.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="solution">Deterministic baselines with seed.yaml</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">LocalCloud provides declarative YAML seeding across 18 supported services—including <code>gcs</code>, <code>pubsub</code>, <code>bigquery</code>, <code>spanner</code>, <code>secretmanager</code>, <code>cloudsql</code>, <code>bigtable</code>, and opt-in <code>firestore</code>.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">Instead of imperatively scripting setup and teardown inside every test file, describe your exact buckets, topics, secrets, and initial table rows once in <code>seed.yaml</code>.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="reset-routes">Reset and reseed in under a second</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">When you need a clean slate, <code>localcloud reset --local-only</code> or <code>POST /reset?project=local-gcp-project</code> wipes project-scoped data inside the running container in ~380 ms—without waiting for a container recreation.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">Pass <code>{`{"restore_seed":true}`}</code> in the reset body and LocalCloud immediately reapplies your project’s last loaded seed fixture so the next run starts from the exact same byte-for-byte baseline.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="try-it">Test a fast reset cycle</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">Start LocalCloud with <a href="/docs/">Getting Started</a>, save this <code>seed.yaml</code>, seed it, and run the reset command. Check <a href="/docs/seed-data/">Seed Data docs</a> for multi-project mappings and startup volume mounting.</p>
        <div class="site-panel mt-5">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
            <span class="site-kicker">seed.yaml</span>
            <CopyButton text={seedYaml} analyticsLabel="copy-blog-reset-seed" />
          </div>
          <pre><code>{seedYaml}</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="site-panel mt-5">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
            <span class="site-kicker">Seed &amp; 1-second restore</span>
            <CopyButton text={resetCmd} analyticsLabel="copy-blog-reset-cmd" />
          </div>
          <pre><code>{resetCmd}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="checklist">Keep fixture resets honest</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">Keep <code>LOCALCLOUD_TERRAFORM_MODE=true</code> separate from seed tests, because Terraform mode intentionally skips seed calls to prevent duplicate resources. Use seed fixtures for fast test state; validate production migrations against real Google Cloud.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BlogLayout>
